{ One system against the whole Sicilian instead of the Open Sicilian's library. Build the big centre with d4; if Black stops it with 2...d5 3.exd5 Qxd5 we are in a Scandinavian structure, and after 2...Nf6 3.e5 the same chain as the Advance lines. The Sicilian is only 15.3% here, so paying Open Sicilian theory for it would be the worst trade in the repertoire. } 1. e4 { → King's Pawn Game } c5 2. c3 { → Sicilian Defense: Alapin Variation, Barmen Defense, Central Exchange } Nc6 { [%eval 0.20] } ( 2... d6 $6 { [%eval 0.55] · trap · 16% play this · they score 48% where 45% is deserved · n=7904 } 3. d4 cxd4 { [%eval 0.56] } 4. cxd4 Nf6 { [%eval 0.76] } ( 4... e6 { [%eval 0.87] } 5. Nf3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } Nf6 { [%eval 0.82] } ( 5... a6 { [%eval 0.85] } 6. Nc3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } b5 { [%eval 1.01] } ( 6... Be7 { [%eval 0.95] } 7. Bd3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play · out of book (0 games) } ) ( 6... Nd7 { [%eval 1.12] } 7. Bd3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play · out of book (0 games) } ) ( 6... Nc6 { [%eval 0.86] } 7. Bd3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play · out of book (0 games) } ) 7. a3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } Bb7 { [%eval 0.61] } 8. Bd3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } ) ( 5... Be7 { [%eval 0.86] } 6. Nc3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } ) ( 5... Nc6 { [%eval 0.83] } 6. Bb5 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } Bd7 { [%eval 0.95] } ( 6... a6 { [%eval 0.68] } 7. Ba4 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } b5 { [%eval 0.40] } 8. Bb3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play · out of book (0 games) } ) 7. O-O { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } a6 { [%eval 0.69] } ( 7... Nf6 { [%eval 0.78] } 8. Nc3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } ) 8. Ba4 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } ) 6. Nc3 { beyond master theory — chosen from club play } ) 5. Nc3 g6 { [%eval